HappyLM is an independent language-model research project.

No proprietary model weights, tokenizer files, training outputs, source code,
trademarks, private datasets, or API-output imitation corpora from Meta,
Anthropic, OpenAI, or Google are included in this repository.

The initial architecture is independently implemented from public research on
decoder-only Transformers, rotary position embeddings, grouped-query
attention, RMS normalization, and SwiGLU feed-forward networks.

PyTorch TorchTitan is used as a public research reference for future scalable
training integration. TorchTitan is distributed under the BSD 3-Clause
License and is not bundled in this initial repository.

HappyLM is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by Meta Platforms,
Anthropic, OpenAI, or Google.
